est ./internal/cmd/...` in my script, it will hang for 10 minutes. That's unacceptable for a test script. I should use `-timeout 60s` at least, or not include cmd tests. The acceptance KR5 explicitly says `-timeout 60s`. So I should run with `-timeout 60s`. But even 60s × (build + runtime + cmd) is acceptable.\n\nBut more importantly: will `go test ./internal/cmd/... -timeout 60s` be GREEN after task4? The task4 scope is migration; it doesn't fix the doing_test hang. So after task4, cmd tests might still fail/hang. That would make my test script fail even after correct implementation. Hmm.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. The KR5 says \"go build + go test ./internal/runtime/... ./internal/cmd/... -timeout 60s 全绿\". This implies task4 SHOULD make cmd tests green (with -timeout 60s). The hang is currently because the doing_test mock isn't isolated. But is fixing that part of task4? The plan says \"迁移测试全绿：cli/executor/agentdir 测试随包迁移（改 package/import 路径）；真实 pi 冒烟测试（realpi/realds）在无 pi 时跳过\". It doesn't explicitly say fix doing_test. But the KR5 acceptance requires cmd tests green.\n\nHmm, let me look at the actual doing_test.go to understand what's happening. Maybe the hang is because the mock pi binary path isn't set up right. Let me examine."}}
